ARM64EC auxiliary delay-load IAT redirection (Wine, partial).

Author: Tim Isaev
Applies to: third_party/src/wine at 54048cbd2bf69aee8cc7be2beb14c5ab63a17842

Carried here because it was written while measuring the second D3D11 title
for issue #11 and would otherwise live only in the untracked Wine checkout.
It is NOT a finished fix and is not built into any committed measurement.

What it does
  - Names the three ARM64EC metadata fields lld actually emits
    (AuxiliaryDelayloadIAT, AuxiliaryDelayloadIATCopy, HybridImageInfoBitfield)
    instead of the __os_arm64x_helper0..2 placeholders.
  - On delay-import resolution, finds the auxiliary delay IAT slot whose
    immutable __impchk_ thunk targets the regular IAT slot just resolved, and
    writes the callee's ARM64EC entry into it.  Later native calls then reach
    ARM64EC code directly instead of the x64 fast-forward thunk.

What it does not do
  - It does not repair the FIRST call.  That call is already in flight through
    the x64 exit thunk when the resolver runs, so a variadic callee still loses
    every argument past the fourth.  See
    ../results/2026-07-25-07-deus-ex-title-scene-blocked.md.

